(7603358, 1228289, 20608, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jfritz27:</b></div><hr/><i> Did you consider posting it in the vertical orientation? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yes I did but I thought it was maybe too obvious like that, as well as portrait orentation would mean some people would have to scroll to see the image.... I added it as a thumbnail in the notes for anyone else who may of missed it.<br/> <br/>When I went down to the quarry edge the huge skull literally ''jumped'' right out at me, I was very lucky, it was autumn colour mixed with deep black still waters, the whole vibe down there was crazy.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2018-11-19 13:42:15.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by jfritz27: Did you consider posting it in the vertical orientation?   Yes I did but I thought it was maybe too obvious like that, as well as portrait orentation would mean some people would have to scroll to see the image.... I added it as a thumbnail in the notes for anyone else who may of missed it. When I went down to the quarry edge the huge skull literally ''jumped'' right out at me, I was very lucky, it was autumn colour mixed with deep black still waters, the whole vibe down there was crazy.', '2018-11-19 13:39:45.000000', '2018-11-19 13:42:15.000000', 0),
